SpyBrowser.Cursory — third-party notices and distribution status

This is an experimental native C# port of cursory-js, a TypeScript port of
Cursory (https://github.com/Vinyzu/cursory). The source references are pinned:
- cursory-js: https://github.com/JWriter20/cursory-js/tree/16fff97fab05bb6b0c6753b2dc136a7692634cec
- Cursory Python: https://github.com/Vinyzu/cursory/tree/5caa9d3477a1ff7b2d413978ea168a93fdc01dfc
The cursory-js commit's LICENSE/NOTICE credits original Cursory © Vinyzu and
cursory-js © Jake Writer, and states LGPL-3.0-or-later for this TypeScript
port. It reports the original work retroactively dual-licensed under
LGPL-3.0-or-later and GPL-3.0-or-later. This C# derivative is distributed
under LGPL-3.0-or-later. The full LGPL and GPL texts are provided as
COPYING.LESSER and COPYING; the LGPL incorporates GPLv3 terms. This package's
own modifications are identified in the corresponding-source documentation.

DATASET — NOT CLEARED FOR EXTERNAL DISTRIBUTION
src/SpyBrowser.Cursory/Data/trajectories.json.gz is byte-for-byte the
cursory-js pinned dataset. The upstream NOTICE attributes recordings to
Margit Antal, Norbert Fejer and Krisztian Buza (SapiMouse,
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9465583) and MIMIC-LOGICS
(MouseSynthesizer, https://github.com/MIMIC-LOGICS/Mouse-Synthesizer), and
asserts redistribution under the original project's license. Those references
and the assertion are preserved as provenance, not treated as independently
verified rights or permission. The dataset's chain of title and redistribution
terms remain unverified. External publication/redistribution is blocked until
that review is resolved. No new human data is collected or introduced here.

